  "issue": {
   "id": 5938305116,
   "url": "https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/issues/364",
   "title": "A working-directory spawn ENOENT is reported as the Claude executable being missing",
   "issue_number": 364,
   "body": "Found by WP-F5 (#102 launch diagnosis) and confirmed by its independent GPT-6.1 Sol review on 2026-10-19. Outside every I01 to I07 bolt; filed for triage.\n\n## Defect\n\nA spawn `ENOENT` caused by the working directory is reported as the executable being missing: Claude preflight says \"The installed Claude executable could not be started\" (`HARNESS_NOT_INSTALLED` class) when the real cause is a working directory the process cannot start in.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Point `TEMP`/`TMP` at a directory whose path is 234 characters or longer (the Claude CLI starts from working directories up to 258 characters and fails from 259; the probe directory adds the rest).\n2. Run `node apps/api/dist/main.js --preflight` or `GET /harness/preflight`.\n\nExpected: a message that names the working directory as the cause, or at least does not claim the executable is missing.\n\nActual: \"The installed Claude executable could not be started\", while `claude --version` works from a short directory.\n\n## Cause\n\n`packages/infrastructure/src/claude/harness.ts:67-70` maps every spawn `ENOENT` to the not-installed class. The same applies to a turn whose run workspace exceeds 258 characters.\n\n## Fix shape\n\nDistinguish a cwd-caused `ENOENT` (check the working directory exists and is startable before spawning, or inspect the error path) from a missing executable, and word the problem accordingly. Coordinate with WP-F1 (#179), which rewrites the readiness classification in the same file.\n\n## Related\n\n#102 (record `docs/qa/2026-10-19-wp-f5-launch-diagnosis.md`), #179.\n",
   "state": "open",
   "user": {
    "login": "Jacob-J-Thomas",
    "name": "Jacob-J-Thomas",
    "email": null,
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92639671?v=4",
    "id": 92639671
   },
   "assignees": null,
